# Line-ending policy: everything in this repo is authored and hashed as LF.
#
# Why this file exists (P1-b, review round 11): several artifacts are pinned by
# sha256 of their *bytes* — the bundled topology references
# (cifkit/data/nets/*-reference.cif, see cifkit/data/nets/*.json cif_sha256) and
# the demo run manifest.  With the Windows default `core.autocrlf=true` a fresh
# clone would check those files out as CRLF, so the hashes (and therefore
# `pytest tests/test_topology_nets.py` and `scripts/verify_demo.py`) failed on
# every clean clone while the developer working copy (checked out as LF) passed.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout byte-identical to what is committed, on every OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly protect byte-pinned and generated artifacts from any EOL rewriting.
cifkit/data/nets/*.json text eol=lf
cifkit/data/nets/*-reference.cif text eol=lf
tests/data/*.cif text eol=lf
runs/** -text
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.xlsx binary
